use to re-deploy modal_app: python -m modal deploy backend/modal_app.py
backend is all in modal, but included in this package for future revisions.
model endpoint is https://adrian-jackson--cranberry-inspector-cranberryinspector-predict.modal.run

One-time setup (before first deploy after the API-key change):
  modal secret create cranberry-api-key API_KEY=<paste a generated key>
  # generate one with: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
Share that same key value with whoever you want to have access — they paste it
into the "access key" prompt the frontend shows on first visit (it's stored in
their browser's localStorage, not baked into the Vercel build).

If SAM3 needs to be updated later, bump SAM3_COMMIT in backend/modal_app.py to
the new commit SHA from https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3 and redeploy.

If a deploy throws ModuleNotFoundError for something SAM3-related after a
SAM3_COMMIT bump: don't assume a package is training-only just because it
"sounds" like it (pycocotools broke this exact way once already — it's
imported unconditionally by sam3.model.sam3_video_base even though we only
use the image path, because model_builder.py imports the whole model
package including video/tracking code). sam3's own pyproject.toml only
declares timm/tqdm/ftfy/regex/iopath/typing_extensions/huggingface_hub as
dependencies — anything else needed has to be listed by hand in both
backend/modal_app.py and pyproject.toml.

To check what's actually needed before guessing: clone SAM3 locally, then
walk the AST of every file reachable from `sam3.model_builder` and
`sam3.model.sam3_image_processor` (the two things backend/pipeline.py
imports), collecting only imports at module top level (not inside function
bodies, which are deferred — that's how a stray `import decord` inside a
video-loading function shows up as "reachable" but isn't actually required).
Cross-reference the result against what's currently pip_install()'d. This is
how the pycocotools/triton/setuptools gap above was actually found and
confirmed, rather than guessed at.